GCP project setup for deployment
================================

One-time prerequisites before either NEON_SQL.howto or CLOUD_SQL.howto can
be followed, and before any Cloud Run deploy will succeed. This document
covers gcloud auth, project creation, API enablement, and the service
accounts used by GitHub Actions and the Cloud Run runtime. Two scripts in
`scripts/` automate most of it; this doc explains what they do, what they
require, and what to fix by hand if something goes wrong.

1. Install and authenticate gcloud
----------------------------------
- Install the Google Cloud SDK: https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install
- Authenticate as a user with permission to create projects and link
  billing in the parent organization (or with Owner/Editor on an existing
  project you intend to reuse):

      gcloud auth login

- If you'll let GitHub Actions push images and deploy, also install the
  GitHub CLI and authenticate it (used by `set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy` to
  set repo secrets):

      brew install gh        # or apt install gh
      gh auth login

2. Create the GCP project and enable APIs
-----------------------------------------
The script `scripts/setup-gcp-project` creates the project, links a
billing account, enables the required APIs, and creates an Artifact
Registry Docker repo:

      ./scripts/setup-gcp-project --project-id=<your-project-id>
      # default region us-central1; pass --region=<region> to change

What it does (idempotent — safe to re-run):

- `gcloud projects create <id>` (skipped if it already exists).
- Picks the first open billing account with `gcloud billing accounts list`
  and links it. If you have multiple billing accounts, link by hand:

      gcloud billing projects link <project-id> --billing-account=<ACCOUNT_ID>

- Enables `run.googleapis.com`, `artifactregistry.googleapis.com`,
  `secretmanager.googleapis.com`.
- Creates an Artifact Registry Docker repository named `container-images`
  in the chosen region.

After this completes you have an empty project with the right APIs on,
but no database and no service accounts yet.

3. Set up the database
----------------------
Pick one:

- Free tier (recommended for first deploy): `docs/NEON_SQL.howto`.
- Cloud SQL: `docs/CLOUD_SQL.howto`.

Either way the result is a `volunteer-call-database-url` Secret in Secret
Manager, and a database seeded with `scripts/initdb/01-schema.sql` and
`scripts/initdb/02-reference-data.sql`.

The order matters: the runtime service account in the next step grants
`roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor` on `volunteer-call-database-url`, so
the secret must exist first.

4. Create deploy + runtime service accounts and GitHub secrets
--------------------------------------------------------------
The script `scripts/set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy` creates two service
accounts and writes the GitHub repo secrets used by the (yet-to-be-ported)
deploy workflow:

      ./scripts/set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy            # create (idempotent)
      ./scripts/set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy --new      # delete and recreate
      ./scripts/set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy --clear    # delete only

Service accounts:

- `github-deploy@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com` — used by CI to push
  images and deploy to Cloud Run. Granted `roles/run.admin`,
  `roles/artifactregistry.writer`, `roles/iam.serviceAccountUser`. The
  script generates a JSON key and writes it to the `GCP_SA_KEY` GitHub
  Actions secret, plus the project id to `GCP_PROJECT`.
- `volunteer-call-runtime@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com` — used by
  Cloud Run at request time. Granted
  `roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor` on `volunteer-call-database-url`.

5. Verify
---------
- Project: `gcloud projects describe <project-id>`
- Required APIs enabled:

      gcloud services list --enabled \
        --filter="name:(run OR artifactregistry OR secretmanager)"

- Artifact Registry repo:

      gcloud artifacts repositories list --location=<region>

- Service accounts:

      gcloud iam service-accounts list

- DATABASE_URL secret accessible by the runtime SA:

      gcloud secrets get-iam-policy volunteer-call-database-url

- GitHub secrets set (from a clone of the repo):

      gh secret list

6. Cleanup
----------
To tear down everything created by these scripts:

      ./scripts/set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy --clear   # SAs + GH secrets
      gcloud projects delete <project-id>             # the whole project

Project deletion is reversible for ~30 days.

7. Other GitHub Actions secrets (forward reference)
---------------------------------------------------
Once a CI/deploy workflow is ported from the rtaff sibling project, two
other secrets are referenced by `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`:

- `GHCR_PAT` — a GitHub Personal Access Token with `write:packages` for
  pushing images to ghcr.io. Create one at
  https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta and set it via:

      gh secret set GHCR_PAT --body '<token>'

- A Codecov token, if coverage upload is wanted (set via `gh secret set
  CODECOV_TOKEN`). Optional.

These are not handled by `set-gcloud-creds-for-deploy` because they are
not GCP credentials.
